      <version name="1.1" author="kallums" time="2026-10-01T12:00:00Z">
        <changelog><![CDATA[Chain your own chords. The chords are now a row you build, up to eight: any of Starting Blocks' 78 named chords (7ths, extended, altered, sus and add, quartal, Tristan, So What and more) or the 9 the scale builds, on any degree. Click a chord to change it, + to add one, - to remove one, or start again from a common progression. Under a chord with notes your scale lacks - a borrowed C major in C minor, a D7 in C major - everything in the catalogue plays the chord's own notes. A smaller window: instruments show a family at a time with the register beside them, and the chord editor opens only while you are changing a chord.]]></changelog>
